:["r2011-draft","tour"],"id":"r2011","next":"rees","read_s":13,"text":"2011 Prairie. The district register reads this house, a neighbour of the Mayer house, as Romanesque: a rough ashlar front, a round-arched entrance and a rounded corner turret under a conical cap."},{"destination":{"id":"rees_house_2110_prairie","kind":"structure"},"evidence":["rees-draft","tour"],"id":"rees","next":"finish","read_s":13,"text":"2110 Prairie. Harriet Rees's narrow house, read by the district register as Cobb and Frost's work of 1888 and as Romanesque: a limestone front under a tall gable that faces the avenue."}],"title":"Romanesque style walk"}
